      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $x>3,$ then ${x}^{2}>9.$\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language, given that $x$ is a real number.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x>3$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}>9$\n\nThen, the given sentence has the following logical structure:\n\n$$\nP(x)⇒Q(x)\n$$\n\nThis, in turn, is equivalent to \n\n$$\n∀\\,x\\in U,\\,P(x)⇒Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere the universal set $U$ is usually apparent from the context. In this case, $x\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, using formal language, our statement reads \n\nFor all real $x,$ if $x>3,$ then ${x}^{2}>9.$\n\nOr, more formally:\n\n$∀\\,x\\in R,\\,(x>3)⇒({x}^{2}>9)$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
