    "q-183712": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183712",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "There exists an integer number such that any natural number is greater than it.\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there exists\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $∃.$\n\n- The word \"any\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to integers and natural numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $k$ and $n,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∀\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nk<n\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,k<n$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
